<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kokand</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kokand is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fergana-valley">Fergana Valley</a> of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a> and was the capital of the Khanate of Kokand from the eighteenth century. The khanate was one of the Central Asian states conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> in the nineteenth century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> annexed Kokand in 1876 as part of its expansion into Turkestan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kokand.jpg" alt="Kokand" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Екатерина Борисова · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B4._%D0%A0%D1%83%D1%81%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%BE-%D0%90%D0%B7%D0%B8%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B1%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BA_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
